==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Bring Area Attackers that can eviscerate all of the Doge variants, including [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]]. This stage poses no threat whatsoever, as it has no pushing power.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
You're gonna want to bring [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] since he can instantly kill 800% Doge Dark at Lv.42. This allows other rushers such as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], to easily rush the base with the help of the [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] [[Cat Combo]]s.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Bring [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] for the Ragin' Gory and either [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] or [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] for the Formicidaean Ariant. The Shibalien Elites can easily be killed by Area Attackers like [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] and [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]]. As for the Wild Doges, [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] should be able to deal with them with some support, and can help with chipping the other Behemoths. Recommended meatshields here are [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]], [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser]] and [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] for tanking the Wild Doges.

